  "goodToKnow": "Die Tugend is virtue: Geduld ist eine Tugend, aus der Not eine Tugend machen (to make a virtue of necessity). Pünktlichkeit, Fleiß, Ordnung and Disziplin are called deutsche Tugenden or Sekundärtugenden; in 1982 politician Oskar Lafontaine provocatively said that with such virtues one could also run a concentration camp, a famous debate. Tugendhaft means virtuous. Plural: die Tugenden."
